1. Executive Summary & Objective
Build a production-grade, fully decoupled Agentic Voice-Cloning and MLOps Pipeline named EchoAgent. The system allows users to engage in a real-time conversational voice session, records and extracts features asynchronously via a message queue, fine-tunes a voice profile, and subsequently unlocks a "Speak to Yourself" bot session where the AI talks back using the user's cloned voice profile.

The primary target is enterprise-grade architecture mastery, flawless MLOps automation, and system design clarity running on a strict bootstrap budget (~₹300–₹500 INR/mo VPS + free cloud layers).

2. Complete User Journey
Landing & Ingestion: User visits the clean frontend (hosted on Cloudflare Pages). They click "Start Conversation".

Real-Time Voice Bot (Session 1): A WebSocket connection opens. A real-time conversational voice bot asks randomized personal questions for 120 seconds to naturally capture prosody, pitch, fillers, and speech rate. Audio is streamed and chunked in real-time.

The Transition & Status Dashboard: At 120 seconds, the call ends. The UI displays an engaging status bar tracking background steps:

Audio Cleaning & Silence Trimming

Mel-Spectrogram & Feature Extraction

Speaker Embedding & Model Training

Registry Validation

The Post-Training Fork: Once background processing completes successfully, the user profile is saved to the DB, and two buttons unlock: [Record Again] and [Speak to Yourself].

The Cloned Bot (Session 2): Clicking [Speak to Yourself] launches a new real-time voice session where the AI agent converses with the user in the user's cloned voice profile.

