6. Engineering Non-Negotiables & Enterprise Standards
Pluggable Model Interface (Strategy Pattern):

Enforce an Abstract Base Class (BaseVoiceProcessor) inside src/core/interfaces.py. The API routing and business logic must never import a specific ML model directly. Upgrading or replacing the core TTS/Voice model later must require changing only a single configuration binding.

Stateless API Gateway:

The FastAPI server must store zero session states in local process memory. All transient sessions and state handoffs go through Redis, allowing horizontal scaling behind a load balancer.

Resilient Asynchronous Queuing:

Raw user voice audio captured over WebSockets must be dumped safely to disk/volume, and a job ID pushed to RabbitMQ. If a worker crashes mid-feature-extraction, Celery must execute exponential backoff retries and route permanently failed jobs to a Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ).

Rigorous MLOps CI/CD:

Every git push must trigger GitHub Actions to run code linters, execute pytest suites against mock audio payloads, build the Docker image, and push artifacts cleanly.